{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_96948120#10_110520620","relevance":2,"reason":"This duplicate/near-duplicate iodomethane passage supports one cause of nematicide loss by saying methyl bromide, a soil disinfectant/nematicide target replaced by iodomethane, was banned under the Montreal Protocol. However, the document is mainly about iodomethane, not dedicated to explaining nematicide losses.","learned":"Methyl bromide’s loss is tied to Montreal Protocol environmental regulation, but this source is not centered on the nematicide-loss question."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"methyl bromide\" (+ nematicide fumigant) (+ phaseout phased-out banned) (+ ozone depletion \"montreal protocol\"))","reason":"Use a tighter methyl bromide/fumigant query to find documents directly explaining that this major nematicide/fumigant was phased out because it depletes ozone under Montreal Protocol rules."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"methyl bromide\" (+ nematicide fumigant) (+ phaseout phased-out banned) (+ ozone depletion \"montreal protocol\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_866237787#0_1763779106","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1482","rank":3,"snippet":"\" , \"end_char\": 1201.000000 , \"headings\": \"Methyl Bromide Methyl Bromide What Is Methyl Bromide? Methyl bromide damages the ozone layer Find more information on methyl bromide: Key Resource The Phaseout of Methyl Bromide Methyl Bromide Alternatives Learn more: Methyl Bromide Critical Uses Methyl Bromide for Quarantine and Preshipment Quarantine Applications Preshipment Applications Apply for a Methyl Bromide Critical Use Exemption Pre-plant application form Post-harvest application form Methyl Bromide Reporting Forms \" , \"segment\": \"Methyl Bromide | <cover>Phaseout of Ozone-Depleting Substances (ODS) | US EPA Methyl Bromide Methyl bromide is a fumigant </cover>used to control pests in agriculture and shipping. Methyl bromide also depletes the ozone layer. Therefore, along with other countries, the United States has phased out production and consumption of methyl bromide with important exceptions for critical uses as well as quarantine and preshipment. Learn more about protecting the ozone layer. Overview Alternatives Critical Uses Quarantine and Preshipment Forms What Is Methyl Bromide? Methyl bromide is an odorless, colorless gas used to control a wide variety of pests in agriculture and shipping, including fungi, weeds, insects, nematodes (or roundworms), and rodents. Agricultural growers ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_96948120#9_110518303","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_96948120#10_110520620","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
