{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_123562181#15_253441264","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage is related to nematicide development and mentions interest in new nematode-control targets with low mammalian toxicity, but it does not explain why many nematicides have been lost, banned, withdrawn, or restricted over recent decades.","learned":"Some new nematicide research seeks low mammalian toxicity, indirectly reflecting toxicity concerns with older chemistries, but this is not direct evidence of nematicide losses."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1536","reason":"The current query has already produced new grade-3 evidence and may still yield additional management documents with direct statements about health, environmental, toxicity, and labeling constraints."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1536"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1797328243#9_3591145964","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1536","rank":10,"snippet":"Garden 1 Nematode Management in the Vegetable Garden 1 What are nematodes? How do nematodes damage plants? Root-Knot Nematodes Ectoparasites Other Nematodes How do I know if nematodes are a problem? Handling Submitting a Sample What can I do about nematodes? Chemical <cover>Nematicides Bionematicides Resistance and Tolerance Soil Solarization Cover Crops Organic Amendments Planting Soil Tillage and Root Destruction Container Growing Summary Tables \" , \"segment\": \"B. Juveniles swell and molt several times. C. Adult female nematode is swollen and starting to lay eggs. D. Root tissue pulled back to show adult female nematode. Credit: Panels A, B, and C, N. A. Sikora UF/IFAS; Panel D, Theresa Friday UF/IFAS Extension How do nematodes damage plants? As plant-parasitic nematodes feed, they damage the root system and reduce the ability of a plant to obtain water and nutrients from the soil. When nematode numbers get high, and/or when environmental </cover>stresses occur, aboveground symptoms may become evident. Aboveground nematode symptoms often resemble nutrient deficiencies or drought stress. Symptoms include yellowing, wilting, and stunting (Figure 7, 8, 9).\" , \"start_char\": 3339.000000 , \"title\": \"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#16_2916726411","rank":5,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_1667865910#17_2916728807","rank":6,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_614024996#15_563342684","rank":7,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_614024996#16_563345009","rank":8,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_508868484#0_571839510","rank":9,"relevance":3}]}}
