{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_164651097#5_387841976","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage is related and gives direct supporting evidence that chemical nematicides are highly toxic and unsuitable for home garden use, which helps explain safety-driven loss or absence of uses. However, the article is a garden/home-use piece rather than a document dedicated to explaining why many nematicides were lost over decades.","learned":"High toxicity made chemical nematicides unsuitable for some home-garden uses, reinforcing health/safety as a reason for reduced availability."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ bromomethane \"methyl bromide\") (+ nematodes nematicide fumigant) (+ \"montreal protocol\" ozone phaseout banned))","reason":"Search for additional direct sources on methyl bromide/bromomethane, a major nematicidal fumigant lost through Montreal Protocol ozone-depletion regulation."}}
